    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da199d23_ddda0671",
        "filename": "src/encode/SkPngEncoderImpl.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 332,
      "author": {
        "id": 6225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-16T08:25:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I added a note about that (along with the strange non-const-ness). In particular:\n* libpng appends the chunks to its internal list of unknown chunks [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/libpng/pngset.c;l\u003d1232;drc\u003debf6d473ea1ee1963abd3afa4e18719b66be0719)\n* and then copies the `data` member [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/libpng/pngset.c;l\u003d1278;drc\u003debf6d473ea1ee1963abd3afa4e18719b66be0719)\n\nThe actual libpng documentation is very unclear on all of this. I carefully verified this behavior on libpng 1.6.22, which we switched to in 2016. Looking at the code before this upgrade ([here](https://codereview.chromium.org/2021403002/diff/230001/third_party/libpng/pngset.c)), it appears this was the behavior before that revision as well.",
      "parentUuid": "f7e45068_4c24616b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 332,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 332,
        "endChar": 30
      },
